@startuml 04-expense-state
' Lifecycle of Expense.status (and how ExpenseApproval rows drive it).
title Expense lifecycle (Expense.status)

[*] --> Decide : createExpense()

state Decide <<choice>>
Decide --> APPROVED : approvers = ∅\n(creator is the only\nparticipant & payer)
Decide --> PENDING : approvers =\n(participants ∪ payer) − creator\n→ one ExpenseApproval + Notification each

state PENDING {
  state "waiting on approvers" as W
  W --> W : an approver APPROVES\n(other approvals still PENDING)
}

PENDING --> APPROVED : last PENDING approval\nis APPROVED
PENDING --> REJECTED : any approver REJECTS\n(reason required →\nrejectionReason, decidedAt)

APPROVED : counted in balances\n& settlement plan
REJECTED : ignored by balances
PENDING : ignored by balances

APPROVED --> [*]
REJECTED --> [*]

note right of PENDING
  Guards in decideExpense():
  • caller must have an ExpenseApproval row
  • expense must still be PENDING
  • caller's decision must still be PENDING
end note
@enduml
